    # v380 (01/10/2026), operator's orders: SH0ES on the Bench; «o teste da transformada radical com as ondas gravitacionais e ecos» (the radical-transform test with gravitational waves and echoes); «todo esse banco de dados novo (gweco) ... já o vincule à bancada» (link the new GW bank to the Bench); «estude tudo que eu já fiz e já escrevemos e resolva os problemas que faltam» (study everything and solve what remains)
    _r0 = core.get("bancada_fases_5_6_7_v380") or {}
    _v0 = lambda d_: str(d_.get("verdict", "n/a")).replace("_", r"\_")
    _nv0 = lambda d_, t_: "" if d_.get("all_verified") is True else (r"\textbf{In this run %s did NOT close: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " % t_)
    _f0 = lambda x_, n_=3: (("%%.%df" % n_) % float(x_)) if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _f5 = _r0.get("fase5") or {}; _f6 = _r0.get("fase6") or {}; _k6 = _f6.get("todos_KMS") or {}; _o6 = _f6.get("o4_KMS_cego") or {}; _m6 = _f6.get("todos_MAY") or {}; _e4 = (_r0.get("emenda_v4") or {}).get("todos_MAY") or {}
    _cm = _f6.get("controles_MAY_v3_z") or {}; _e5 = _r0.get("emenda_v5") or {}; _d5 = _e5.get("todos_DEC") or {}; _d5o = _e5.get("o4_DEC_cego") or {}; _lab = lambda s_: str(s_ or "n/a").replace("TGL_ECHO_RADICAL_V3__", "").replace("_", r"\_")
    _f7 = _r0.get("fase7") or {}; _tz = _f7.get("T_z_ganho") or {}; _lb = _f7.get("U_lnB_sombra_vs_acumulada") or {}; _gb = _r0.get("gw_bank") or {}; _gs = _gb.get("status") or {}; _va = _f5.get("validacao") or {}; _p5 = _f5.get("P_sombra") or {}
    s.append(r"\paragraph*{Beside (v380) --- Phases 5, 6 and 7 of the Bench, read by hash: SH0ES, the echo as the radical response of the boundary, the chronometers with full covariance; the gravitational-wave bank; the errata beside.} " + _nv0(_r0, "the Bench reading") +
             r"With no new kernel and the gate untouched, the program reads by hash (bytes and LF-normalised text, side by side; " + str(len(_r0.get("crlf_differs") or [])) + r" artefact with CRLF, stated) the pre-registrations, the powers recorded before opening (V3, V4 and V5) and the results of three Bench phases (01/10/2026). "
             r"\textbf{Phase 5 (SH0ES on the Bench):} the full Pantheon+SH0ES (1657 SNe, 77 Cepheid calibrators in 37 hosts, $1701\times1701$ covariance, profiled $M$) gives $H_0=" + _f0(_va.get("H0"), 2) + r"\pm" + _f0(_va.get("sigma_H0"), 2) + r"$ ($z=" + _f0(_va.get("z_vs_alvo"), 2) + r"$ from the published $73.6\pm1.1$, \textsf{[DECLARED]}, not re-read at the source); in the ``shadow'' reading (distance readers read the constant factor $K$ at every $z$) the ladder deviation is $z_\delta=" + _f0(_p5.get("z_delta"), 2) + r"$. "
             r"\textbf{Phase 6 (ECHO V3, ``the radical transform''):} the root enters as the pre-registered \emph{amplitude} of the boundary's response to the merger--ringdown burst (the Elementary Reason, v379), in three readings --- $\sqrt{\bTGL}$ (weight 1), $\sin 2\theta_M=2\sqrt{\bTGL(1-\bTGL)}$ (the graviton reads at $2\theta$, \textsf{[CONJECTURE]}) and $\bTGL$ --- and two delay laws \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}: MAY, $\tau=(2GM_f/c^3)\ln(1/\bTGL)$, and KMS, $\tau=2\pi/\kappa(M_f,a_f)$ per event. "
             r"Pre-registered sample: 244 BBH from O1--O4 (67 from the May cache + 177 from O4 downloaded from GWOSC), 484 hashed series; the anchored estimator corrected after the 28/09 audit (per-event final spin, shifted-delay nulls, injections with sampled parameters at the catalogue amplitude, coherent H1+L1 combination, jackknife, BBH only). "
             r"Result: the pair $(\sqrt{\bTGL}\ \text{or}\ \sin 2\theta_M,\ 2\pi/\kappa)$ is \texttt{FALSIFIED\_AT\_DELAY\_LAW} in " + str(_k6.get("n_eventos", "n/a")) + r" BBH ($\hat a=" + _f0(_k6.get("a")) + r"\pm" + _f0(_k6.get("sigma_usado")) + r"$ in units of $\sqrt{\bTGL}$; $z_{\rm excl}=" + _f0(_k6.get("z_excl_R1"), 1) + r"$ and $" + _f0(_k6.get("z_excl_R2"), 1) + r"$; relative systematics " + _f0(_k6.get("sist_rel_R1"), 2) + r" and " + _f0(_k6.get("sist_rel_R2"), 2) + r"$\le0.3$; mute controls) and in the \emph{blind O4 subsample} (" + str(_o6.get("n_eventos", "n/a")) + r" of the " + str(_k6.get("n_eventos", "n/a")) + r", not an independent replica: $z_{\rm excl}=" + _f0(_o6.get("z_excl_R1"), 1) + r"$ and $" + _f0(_o6.get("z_excl_R2"), 1) + r"$; the May part, not blind, gives $\sqrt{\bTGL}$ underpowered and $\sin 2\theta_M$ falsified); "
             r"the MAY law stays \texttt{INCONCLUSIVE\_SYSTEMATICS} by the rule (short delay: template mismatch up to " + _f0(_m6.get("sistematica_abs"), 2) + r"), and in V3 its $\tau/2$ control responded at $" + _f0((_cm.get("todos") or {}).get("x0.5"), 1) + r"\sigma$ (all) and $" + _f0((_cm.get("o4") or {}).get("x0.5"), 1) + r"\sigma$ (O4) --- the pre-registered flag \texttt{DELAY\_CONTROL\_RESPONDS} was not written by the pipeline and is stated here (look-elsewhere by definition; the post hoc diagnostic attributes the response to template mismatch induced at $\tau/2$); "
             r"amendment V4 (a $\pm2\sigma$ grid, not blind, stated) takes $(\sin 2\theta_M,\ \text{MAY})$ to falsified ($z_{\rm excl}=" + _f0(_e4.get("z_excl_R2"), 1) + r"$) with the controls at " + _f0(_e4.get("controles_max_z"), 1) + r"$\sigma$ (just below the flag, stated), and $(\sqrt{\bTGL},\ \text{MAY})$ stays inconclusive as the limit of this estimator --- no third amendment without a new estimator (rule V4). "
             r"Amendment V5, blind \emph{only} to the new law (V3 and V4 already opened), tested the delay law of 24/12/2025 from the archive, $\tau=2GM_f/(\bTGL c^3)$ ($\approx14$ periods; \textsf{[DECLARED]}: derived by an AI under the operator's direction, not derived from the axiom; never opened at that delay): the radical readings are falsified there as well ($z_{\rm excl}=" + _f0(_d5.get("z_excl_R1"), 1) + r"$ and $" + _f0(_d5.get("z_excl_R2"), 1) + r"$; O4 $" + _f0(_d5o.get("z_excl_R1"), 1) + r"$ and $" + _f0(_d5o.get("z_excl_R2"), 1) + r"$; mute controls); the document's own pair (amplitude $\bTGL$) has no power in this estimator (" + _f0(_d5.get("poder_R3"), 1) + r"$\sigma$; blind power recorded before opening " + _f0(_e5.get("poder_R3_cego"), 1) + r"$\sigma$): the label emitted by the general rule is \texttt{" + _lab(_e5.get("R3_rotulo_emitido")) + r"} (systematics relative to the tiny amplitude $>0.3$), and the V5 clause of the amendment (power $<5\sigma\Rightarrow$ \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED\_UNDERPOWERED}) was not applied by the pipeline --- a stated deviation; underpowered, not falsified. "
             r"The fourth archive law, $2GM/(\alpha^2c^3)$ (4--12 s), lies outside the 2.5-s segment and was not tested. Falsifying the \emph{pair} (reading, law) does not falsify the theory: the delay laws are not derived from the axiom; the December ``100$\sigma$'' stays retired (v340). "
             r"\textbf{Phase 7 (chronometers with the Moresco+2020 covariance):} with the IMF and SPS-model terms correlated across the 15 Moresco points (source values), the $z$ of the accumulated-law gain in the intermediate registers goes from $" + _f0(_tz.get("diagonal"), 2) + r"$ (diagonal) to $" + _f0(_tz.get("moresco2020"), 2) + r"$, and $\ln B$(shadow/accumulated) from $" + _f0(_lb.get("diagonal"), 2) + r"$ to $" + _f0(_lb.get("moresco2020"), 2) + r"$: the Phase 4--5 readings \emph{weaken} --- the ``diagonal errors'' caveat is now measured. "
             r"\textbf{The bank:} " + str(_gb.get("n_ok", "n/a")) + r" of " + str(_gb.get("n_jobs", "n/a")) + r" O4 series from GWOSC OK by sha256 manifest (" + str(_gs.get("NAN_IN_WINDOW", "n/a")) + r" NaN in the window, one detector per event; " + str(_gs.get("WINDOW_OUTSIDE_FILE", "n/a")) + r" windows outside the file); the resident bank lives in Bench One (API, MCP), the templates and the fit in WSL, and the program only reads. "
             r"\textbf{Six errata beside} from the 28/09 audit (CT-03/GWECO-04: the $\sqrt{\bTGL}$ amplitude of rites v341--v348 is the weight-1 one, \textsf{[INPUT]}; GWECO-05: $2\pi/\kappa$ is a period in imaginary time; GWECO-03; RD-06; VV-N1: the NuFIT entry contains JUNO and the tension depends on the global fit, $2.95\sigma$ against $2.44\sigma$; RNC-06), plus the erratum of the diagonal line of v378 and the note on the bank. The delay law and the weight of the boundary's response to the graviton are the operator's to decide. Proved $\neq$ confirmed; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} $\neq$ \texttt{CONFIRMED}. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v0(_r0) + r"}.")
